  "text": "Let's break down the problem step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Interpret the given equations\n\n1. The first equation is \\( |25 + 20i - z| = 5 \\). This represents a circle in the complex plane with center \\( 25 + 20i \\) and radius \\( 5 \\).\n\n2. The second equation is \\( |z - 4 - k| = |z - 3i - k| \\). This represents the set of points equidistant from the points \\( 4 + k \\) and \\( 3i + k \\) in the complex plane. The set of points equidistant from two points is the perpendicular bisector of the line segment joining those two points.\n\n### Step 2: Find the perpendicular bisector of the segment joining \\( 4 + k \\) and \\( 3i + k \\)\n\nThe midpoint of the segment joining \\( 4 + k \\) and \\( 3i + k \\) is:\n\\[ \\frac{(4 + k) + (3i + k)}{2} = \\frac{4 + k + 3i + k}{2} = \\frac{4 + 3i + 2k}{2} = 2 + \\frac{3}{2}i + k \\]\n\nThe slope of the line segment joining \\( 4 + k \\) and \\( 3i + k \\) is:\n\\[ \\text{slope} = \\frac{(3i + k) - (4 + k)}{3i + k - (4 + k)} = \\frac{3i - 4}{3i - 4} = -1 \\]\n\nThe perpendicular bisector will have a slope that is the negative reciprocal of \\(-1\\), which is \\(1\\). The equation of the perpendicular bisector is:\n\\[ y - (2 + \\frac{3}{2}i + k) = 1(x - (2 + \\frac{3}{2}i + k)) \\]\n\\[ y - 2 - \\frac{3}{2}i - k = x - 2 - \\frac{3}{2}i - k \\]\n\\[ y = x \\]\n\nSo, the perpendicular bisector is the line \\( y = x \\).\n\n### Step 3: Find the intersection of the circle and the line \\( y = x \\)\n\nSubstitute \\( y = x \\) into the equation of the circle:\n\\[ |25 + 20i - x - xi| = 5 \\]\n\\[ |25 + 20i - x(1 + i)| = 5 \\]\n\\[ |(25 + 20i) - x(1 + i)| = 5 \\]\n\\[ |25 + 20i - x - xi| = 5 \\]\n\\[ |(25 - x) + (20 - x)i| = 5 \\]\n\\[ \\sqrt{(25 - x)^2 + (20 - x)^2} = 5 \\]\n\\[ (25 - x)^2 + (20 - x)^2 = 25 \\]\n\\[ 625 - 50x + x^2 + 400 - 40x + x^2 = 25 \\]\n\\[ 2x^2 - 90x + 950 = 25 \\]\n\\[ 2x^2 - 90x + 925 = 0 \\]\n\\[ x^2 - 45x + 462.5 = 0 \\]\n\n### Step 4: Solve the quadratic equation\n\nThe discriminant of the quadratic equation \\( x^2 - 45x + 462.5 = 0 \\) is:\n\\[ \\Delta = 45^2 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 462.5 = 2025 - 1850 = 175 \\]\n\nThe solutions to the quadratic equation are:\n\\[ x = \\frac{45 \\pm \\sqrt{175}}{2} = \\frac{45 \\pm 5\\sqrt{7}}{2} \\]\n\nSo, the solutions are:\n\\[ x = \\frac{45 + 5\\sqrt{7}}{2} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad x = \\frac{45 - 5\\sqrt{7}}{2} \\]\n\n### Step 5: Find the corresponding \\( y \\) values\n\nSince \\( y = x \\), the corresponding \\( y \\) values are the same as the \\( x \\) values.\n\n### Step 6: Find the values of \\( k \\)\n\nThe solutions to the system of equations are the points on the circle that lie on the line \\( y = x \\). The solutions to the quadratic equation give us the \\( x \\) and \\( y \\) coordinates of these points. The values of \\( k \\) are the real parts of these points.\n\nThe solutions to the quadratic equation are:\n\\[ x = \\frac{45 + 5\\sqrt{7}}{2} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad x = \\frac{45 - 5\\sqrt{7}}{2} \\]\n\nSo, the values of \\( k \\) are:\n\\[ k = 2 + \\frac{3}{2}i + \\frac{45 + 5\\sqrt{7}}{2} = \\frac{55 + 5\\sqrt{7}}{2} \\]\n\\[ k = 2 + \\frac{3}{2}i + \\frac{45 - 5\\sqrt{7}}{2} = \\frac{53 - 5\\sqrt{7}}{2} \\]\n\nThe sum of all possible values of \\( k \\) is:\n\\[ \\frac{55 + 5\\sqrt{7}}{2} + \\frac{53 - 5\\sqrt{7}}{2} = \\frac{55 + 53}{2} = \\frac{108}{2} = 54 \\]\n\nSo, the sum of all possible values of \\( k \\) is \\( 54 \\). The final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{54} \\]",
